      "speaker_notes": "Behavior Driven Development (Gherkin) vs Test Driven Development.",
      "html_content": "<div style=\"display:grid; grid-template:1fr / 1fr 1fr; gap:20px; height:100%;\">\n  <div style=\"background:var(--card-bg-from); border:1px solid var(--accent-1); border-radius:var(--card-radius); padding:24px; display:flex; flex-direction:column; padding:32px;\">\n    <h2 style=\"font-family:var(--display-font); color:var(--text-primary); font-size:32px;\">Pruebas Manuales / TDD</h2>\n    <ul style=\"color:var(--text-secondary); font-size:18px; margin-top:20px; line-height:1.8;\">\n      <li>Susceptible a error humano</li>\n      <li>Tedioso y repetitivo</li>\n      <li>Difícil de escalar</li>\n    </ul>\n  </div>\n  <div style=\"background:var(--card-bg-from); border:1px solid var(--accent-2); border-radius:var(--card-radius); padding:24px; display:flex; flex-direction:column; padding:32px;\">\n    <h2 style=\"font-family:var(--display-font); color:var(--text-primary); font-size:32px;\">Automatizadas / BDD</h2>\n    <ul style=\"color:var(--text-secondary); font-size:18px; margin-top:20px; line-height:1.8;\">\n      <li>Ejecución rápida y repetible</li>\n      <li>Liberan tiempo para testing exploratorio</li>\n      <li>Integración continua (CI/CD)</li>\n    </ul>\n  </div>\n</div>"
    },
